  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "n-atlas-1",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Reading order: Atlas → Ontology → Views → Library → Machinery → Crates. Each artboard names its sources (canon path or reference repo + commit). Nothing here schedules construction; the roadmap is CONS1 and UAR is frozen.",
      "page": "page-atlas"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-atlas-2",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 200,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Starred references (paperproof, MorphoHDL, OpenSCAD, SolveSpace, KiCad) each own at least one Views artboard and one Machinery artboard; the five others contribute rows to Library 0, Machinery 3/6/7 and this matrix.",
      "page": "page-atlas"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-views-1",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 320,
      "text": "Twelve faces of one workspace. Each artboard is a low-fidelity wireframe: boxes and labels are real (types, ids, receipts), positions are not. Species colour tells you what a control does; a dashed border is an obstruction that stays visible.",
      "page": "page-views"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-ontology-1",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 320,
      "text": "Type sheets are readings of canon definitions with path:line citations. The Crate page says which existing Rust/Lean owner already carries each one.",
      "page": "page-ontology"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-library-1",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 320,
      "text": "Every component is a KiCad-style triple (symbol · footprint · model) plus a MorphoHDL rule with a fallback and SolveSpace-style constraints. Library 0 is the contact-rule matrix every net is checked against.",
      "page": "page-library"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-machinery-1",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 320,
      "text": "Pipelines lifted from the references and retyped: each stage carries its species; the boundary panel says what canon refuses.",
      "page": "page-machinery"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-archive-1",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 320,
      "text": "The previous draft (The descent at five) and the cached prototypes, unchanged. Their vocabulary — species colours, box kinds, STIX/Plex faces — is what the new pages inherit.",
      "page": "page-archive"
    },
    {
      "id": "n-crates-1",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 320,
      "text": "Grade of this page: interpretation. It names existing owners by exact path and the absent types by exact field; it schedules nothing. The roadmap's CONS2 size ratchets would govern any of these modules.",
      "page": "page-crates"
    }
  ],
